774 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Materiality analysis has become a fundamental tool in recent years for organisations pursuing sustainability goals. As companies embark on their individual journeys towards corporate social responsibility \(CSR\), this approach plays a pivotal role. Through the development of a Materiality Matrix, a visual representation derived from internal and/or external analysis, companies pinpoint the most significant sustainability aspects for both themselves and their stakeholders. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
775 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The process of constructing the materiality matrix began with the selection of the most relevant topics for our company and our main stakeholders: management, employees, suppliers, clients, local entities, and institutions. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
777 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The topics were selected based on careful listening and analysis of internal company sources \(objectives, strategies and company policies, reporting documentation, feedback from customers and suppliers\) as well as monitoring of external inputs \(guidelines and standards ISO 26000:2010, Agenda 2030, GRI Standard, legislative sources and evaluation of industry trends\). In choosing which topics to consider meterially impactful for our organisation, we endeavoured to answer two guiding questions:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
778 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1786 0 R
/ActualText (Which topic is relevant for my organisation \(based on its purpose, activities, organisational model, operating context, and the awareness and orientation of internal stakeholders\)? )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
779 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1787 0 R
/ActualText (Which topic is relevant for our external stakeholders \(considering their attention to the topic, the area of impact, and the area in which the stakeholders are particularly active\)?)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
780 0 obj
<<
