/S /H1
/T (IMPACT TABLE - SOCIAL)
/E (IMPACT TABLE - SOCIAL)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
783 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The social dimension represents the totality of conditions contributing to human well-being. This includes security, health, education, democratic participation, and equitable access to justice. Fair distribution across social classes, genders, and geographical and cultural backgrounds is fundamental for the proper evolution of social development and the flourishing of communities. Building upon the social dimension, the 2030 Agenda advocates for a broader approach. Its focus lies on actions that affirm economic, social, political, and cultural rights for everyone, ensuring gender and racial equality. Additionally, it prioritises initiatives that safeguard the traditions and rights of local communities within their own territories.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
784 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The essential characteristic of Social Responsbility is the willingness of an organisation to integrate social considerations into its decision-making processes and to be accountable for the impacts of its decisions and activities on society. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
