/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To improve the transparency and consistency of our emmisions data over time, we will be adopting the Scope 1 and Scope 2 classification methodologies. This approach will allow for a more comprehensive assessment of our sustainability performance, including comparisons with industry peers. By differentiating between direct emissions \(Scope 1\) arising from our own energy use and internal processes, and indirect emissions \(Scope 2\) resulting from the purchase of electricity and heat from external sources, we can identify and evaluate the environmental impact of our activities more accurately.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1031 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1890 0 R
/ActualText (TRACKING, REPORTING AND OFFSETTING)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1032 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In 2024, we are committed to developing comprehensive social and environmental impact reports. These will encompass details on our CO2 emissions, including monitoring methodologies, reporting frameworks, and offsetting strategies.  We can achieve this goal through a variety of activities, such as investing in reforestation projects, promoting renewable energy, and purchasing carbon credits. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1033 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Our goal is to promote transparency by publishing periodic reports detailing our energy consumption and environmental impact, including total CO2 emissions, a breakdown of our primary emission sources, and actions undertaken to reduce them. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
